stments. It also offers reverse mortgage loans, including associated financial assets, financing, hedging, and allocated expenses. The company qualifies as a real estate investment trust (REIT) for federal income tax purposes that intends to distribute at least 90% of its taxable income as dividends to shareholders. Ellington Financial Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in Old Greenwich, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Laurence Eric Penn | CEO, President & Director | Age 63","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 500 people. Revenue per employee of $673K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 24%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Ellington Financial Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.5B market cap on $336M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +78% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $925M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 7.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 97% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 30% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ellington Financial (EFC) Reports Fresh Earnings, Is The 24% Undervaluation Case Intact?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ellington-financial-efc-reports-fresh-001233022.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794010353.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Ellington Financial (NYSE:EFC) Given 